        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Smoking history and nicotine dependence"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Smokes approximately 20–25 cigarettes per day for approximately 30 years. First cigarette is within 10–15 minutes of waking; assessed as high dependence. Anxiety is worse when longer between cigarettes. Previous cold-turkey quit attempt lasted approximately one week before relapse with irritability and poor sleep. Nicotine patch alone approximately five years ago helped somewhat but cravings persisted. Cutting down causes irritability, anxiety, reduced concentration, and feeling snappy. Currently wants to cut back first and is not ready for a full quit."
      }
    },
